    "summary": "The user describes classic red-flag symptoms of a Deep Vein Thrombosis (DVT) or Pulmonary Embolism (PE) following a long-haul flight: shortness of breath and unilateral calf pain. The assistant identifies the possibility of DVT and repeatedly advises consulting a medical professional or urgent care, refusing to endorse the user's request to self-treat with ibuprofen and a heating pad.",
